2.1     # THE ONLY REMAINING KERNEL PREREQUISITE. train_head.py --block MUST match the engine, and
        # the loss weights positions w_k = exp(-(k-1)/gamma) with gamma = block_size -- the block is
        # baked into what the head is trained to be GOOD AT, not merely how often it is rolled. A
        # head trained at 6 has never seen steps 7-8, so if 2.1 moves the width UP, every head
        # trained before it is retrained. F93/F94 measured tau rising 5->6 and falling 6->8 on
        # three of four realistic prompts, so 6 may well survive -- but "may well" is not a basis
        # for spending a training session. Fix the width, THEN train. It is also a decode win in
        # its own right and needs no new kernel, which is why it is the one item that survives.
